+# Third pass: residential streets toward 10 km — 2026-11-11
+
+Newly dated: 10,702.47 m in 53 persistent street objects (EPSG:3874), all new. No existing road was confirmed or changed, so nothing overlaps the first or second pass. Each object is one modern street section; streets made of several OSM ways (Nabbvägen, Solvändan, Norrbölevägen, Skarpansvägen, Skeppargatan, Skiljevägen, Servicegatan) are one continuous line, so no parallel carriageways are counted.
+
+| First reviewed evidence | Newly dated metres |
+| --- | ---: |
+| 1968 | 4,742.89 |
+| 1978 (red overprint revision) | 192.10 |
+| 1985 | 5,086.41 |
+| 1995 | 681.07 |
+
+| Area | Metres | Streets and first evidence |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Johannebo, east and west of Godbyvägen | 2,739.27 | 1968: Krokensvägen, Grantorpsvägen, Ängsvägen, Verkstadsvägen, Fridhemsvägen, Johannebovägen, Nabbvägen, Sanatorievägen, Mellangårdsvägen (southern part; whole street from 1985). 1985: Strandhagsvägen, Dalgränd, Bastugränd. 1995: Doktorsvägen |
+| Hindersböle | 4,442.96 | 1968: Ljungvägen, Askuddsvägen. 1985: the residential grid (Solvändan, Blomstervägen, Högbackagatan, Backavägen, Movägen, Sandåsvägen, Lillåkersvägen and twelve gränder). 1995: Odalvägen, Odalgränd, Riåkersgränd |
+| Norrböle, north of Bolstavägen | 1,545.89 | 1985: Karlbergsvägen, Skogshyddsvägen, Dalkarbyvägen, Norrbölevägen |
+| Skarpans and Servicegatan | 1,386.86 | 1968: Skarpansvägen (a red main road), Skeppargatan, Skiljevägen, Gesällgatan. 1978: Servicegatan's northern loop |
+| Västernäs | 446.06 | 1968: Stenhuggarvägen, Smedsgränd |
+| Stenliden | 141.43 | 1985: Västra Stenliden |
+
+## Findings
+
+**Johannebo was already a street grid in 1968.** Krokensvägen, Grantorpsvägen and the streets east of Godbyvägen are drawn with houses on both sides in 1968, and in the same place in every later edition. Strandhagsvägen is not one of them. In 1968 its two rows of houses stand back to back on a property line; the road then was the way to the fisheries school about 30 m further south, which is a footpath today. Strandhagsvägen therefore starts in 1985, and the school road is not dated here. Mellangårdsvägen is shown only from Godbyvägen to Fridhemsvägen in 1968 and 1978. Its object shows that part as a partial extent (a substring of the modern line ending at the Fridhemsvägen junction) and the whole street from 1985.
+
+**Hindersböle's grid is a 1985 addition around two older lanes.** In 1968 and 1978 the area is fields, plots and the farm lanes around Stentorpa. Two of those lanes lie where modern streets are, within about 10 m: Ljungvägen (with its link north to Lillåkersvägen) and Askuddsvägen (the old road south from Hindersböle to Lemlandsvägen). Both start in 1968. The other 22 streets are first drawn in 1985, and Odalvägen with its gränder in 1995 (fields, Ättehögar, in 1985). An older road about 30 m west of Blomstervägen's southern part is recorded as unclear evidence, not as Blomstervägen.
+
+**Thin red 1978 lines are not counted as streets.** The 1978 overprint draws new roads in thick red, like Rökerirondellen and Österleden. Along several later streets (Högbackagatan, Movägen, Sandåsvägen, Prästkragegränd, Lillåkersvägen, Karlbergsvägen, Skogshyddsvägen, Dalkarbyvägen, Norrbölevägen) it has only a thin red line. Those may be plot or plan boundaries, so 1978 is recorded as *unclear* and the streets start in 1985. Servicegatan's loop is drawn in the thick overprint and starts in 1978.
+
+## Method and data
+
+The review used per-street contact sheets made from the original scans: one row per modern way, with 1968 shown once with the way outlined and then the unmarked 1968, 1978, 1985 and 1995 crops of the same ground. Area crops, labelled overlays and zooms were used where a sheet was not decisive. The overlays only help find the place; every decision rests on the unmarked crops. Sheets, crops and helper scripts are in `data/map-scan-cache/review/mariehamn-major-roads/pass3/` (`waysheet.py`, `crop.py`, `labels.py`, `zoom.py`); `reviewSheets` in the review file lists each sheet with its SHA-256.
+
+`data/mariehamn-street-pass3.json` is generated by `pass3/prepare.py`, which checks ownership against the pre-pass snapshot `pass3/before.json.gz`. The script captures input hashes and is kept for audit, so do not rerun it blindly. Each decision stores its modern members with hashes, the city-stage copies it owns, the 2014/2021/2025 originals (or which years have none), the four observations, its geometry phases and its counted length.
+
+`scripts/mariehamn_street_pass3.py` runs after the Lemlandsvägen split. It uses the second pass's validator and writer, now `apply_reviewed_streets` in `scripts/mariehamn_major_road_followups.py`, with its own id prefix, geometry prefix and marker (`mariehamnStreetPass3`). The second pass calls the same function with its original settings, so its output is unchanged. All matching happens at build time.
+
+## Deferred
+
+These are listed in the review file and stay undated:
+
+- Streets that are a narrow lane or path in 1985, a black line rather than a red street in 1995, or that connect today only through footways and cycleways: Myrstigen, Betesgränd, Bättringsvägen, Hälsostigen, Kasbrinken, Kärrstigen, the southern stub of Johannebovägen, Martallsvägen, the western part of Kråkbärsstigen. They need the road-to-path state model.
+- Streets present by 1985 or 1995 that reach the dated network only through junction pieces that are still undated (Västra Utfarten's carriageways, Doktorsvägen's service section): Uppgårdsvägen, Östra Stenliden, the eastern part of Kråkbärsstigen, Varvsvägen, Framnäsvägen. Dating them alone would draw streets that end short of the network.
+- Trädgårdsvägen and Åkervägen (single lines in 1968, and Åkervägen connects only through Trädgårdsvägen), Mjölnargränd (only partly visible in 1968), and Kilvägen, Lagervägen, Marielundsvägen, Villagränd, Bogränd, Snesgränd and Servicegatan's southern part, where the position or connection is unclear in at least one edition.
+- Streets absent up to 1995: Nygårdsvägen, Årsringen, Kärnveden, Torksprickan, Kummelgränd.
+
+## Validation
+
+The catalogue at the start of the pass is `pass3/before.json.gz`, identical to the published catalogue after the Lemlandsvägen split. `pass3/audit.py` rebuilds the catalogue with the pass disabled and confirms that the baseline equals that snapshot. Against it, the pass adds 53 objects and 289 geometries, all with the pass's prefix, and one source. No existing object, geometry or city stage changes, and no source feature gains a second owner. The result is in `pass3/scope-audit.json`.
+
+`tests/mariehamn-street-pass3.test.cjs` checks:
+
+- the totals, counted once by first edition;
+- that each street starts at its first reviewed edition, and that an unclear or absent earlier edition never moves the start;
+- one stable geometry from 1995 to 2026, drawn once per city stage;
+- single ownership of members and city-stage copies, and that deferred streets stay unowned;
+- Mellangårdsvägen's partial extent;
+- that every street joins a road drawn in its first edition (this check found Åkervägen, Uppgårdsvägen, Varvsvägen and the others listed above as deferred);
+- the Hindersböle, Servicegatan and Skarpansvägen dates.
+
+`tests/test_mariehamn_street_pass3.py` checks that the review applies once, matches the build, needs the second pass, and rejects early starts, a present edition before the start, wrong partial extents, a partial geometry without a partial observation, double ownership, discontinuous sections, changed inputs and wrong lengths, each without touching the catalogue. `tests/temporal-objects.test.cjs` counts the new identities.
+
+**Publication.** Deployed 2026-11-11 as Cloudflare version `167275da-4c53-4517-a19b-fc820fcd773e`. The release was prepared from the live version (`074f8450…`) plus only this pass: the catalogue, `assets/mariehamn-street-pass3.json`, the loader card in `index.html`, and cache stamps in `temporal-objects.js` and `object.html`. Other unpublished workspace changes were left out. All 286 live files were checked byte for byte against the release; see `pass3/deployment.json`.
